# WHERE  :  """ Using WHERE() in Filtering Columns """
==============================================
""" 📍 $ Filtering Fat Content = Regular
    📍$ Slicing the Data with item Type = Soft Drinks & Weight < 10
    📍$ Fetching the data with Tier in (Tier1 or Tier 2) and Outlet Size is NULL """

   -----------------------
🗿 WHERE() Scenario 1
   -----------------------

🎮  df.filter(col("Col 1")=='variable name').display()
🎮  df.filter(col("Item_Fat_Content")=='Regular').display()

   -----------------------
🗿 WHERE() Scenario 2  """ Multi-Column Filtering """
   -----------------------

🎮  df.filter((col("Col 1")=='Soft Drinks') & (col("Col 2")<10)).display()

   -----------------------
🗿 WHERE() Scenario 3   utilise .isin() & .isNull()   """ Multi-Column Filtering """
   -----------------------

🎮  df.filter((col("Outlet_Size").isNull() & col("Outlet_Location_Type").isin('Tier 1','Tier 2'))).display()


